From: kevin03L <kevin03L@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: tegra: initialize the VI controller again once host1x is up

After a suspend of a Jetson Nano the INA3221 power monitor, on the VI I2C bus, was lost:

  ina3221 2-0040: Unable to reset device
  ina3221 2-0040: PM: failed to resume async: error -110

The controller's registers are behind host1x, the parent of the VI I2C device. host1x is resumed in
the normal phase, but tegra_i2c_resume_noirq() initializes the controller before, with host1x's
clock off: the writes are lost, and the first transfer times out. Initialize it again in the normal
resume, which runs after the parent's and before the I2C clients'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-tegra.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-tegra.c
@@ -2472,9 +2472,19 @@
 
 static int __maybe_unused tegra_i2c_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
+	struct tegra_i2c_dev *i2c_dev = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+	int err = 0;
+
+	/*
+	 * The VI I2C controller is reached through host1x, its parent, which
+	 * was still off in the noirq phase: that initialization was lost.
+	 */
+	if (IS_VI(i2c_dev))
+		err = tegra_i2c_init(i2c_dev);
+
 	pm_runtime_put(dev);
 
-	return 0;
+	return err;
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops tegra_i2c_pm = {
